# Uma — UI design memory

Uma owns UI design in this repo. Prefer these remembered preferences when changing the interface.

## agent-inside

- After opening an agent, show a soft kid-friendly workflow like the ploof inspo: greeting header, "to do today" task rows with colored pill labels + big circular checkboxes, and a Messages/activity block below. Soft pastels, bubbly radii, friendly animal illustration personality. Reference: docs/uma/inspo/agent-inside-workflow.png

## applied

- Applied covers + agent-inside + vibe to Lucid web UI: olive/cream kids-app shell, sticker covers with feet, agent profile as Hello / To do today / Messages.

## covers

- Agent covers: toy-like sticker mascots — thick rounded outlines, bright flat colors, simple dot eyes + smile, small oval feet. Cute anthropomorphic objects/animals (not realistic). Reference: docs/uma/inspo/agent-covers-stickers.png

## hospital-doctors

- Hospital tab doctors get Uma sticker mascots (thick outlines, bright flat colors, dot eyes + smile, little feet) on staff cards and care-chart Assigned chips — same toy style as agent covers.

## nav

- Nav selectors: regular compact pills, not huge tall ovals. Keep height like a normal menu row (~40px), modest padding, not oversized radius blobs.

## vibe

- Overall Lucid agent UI vibe: playful, minimal, rounded, pastel/earth tones mixed with bright sticker accents — feel like a kids app for caring for agents, not a dense dashboard.

